    <bpmn:process id="W_W3490" name="W3490. Remodel Staff Training &amp; Change Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Pre re-opening (W3489); new systems/assortment
Frequency: Per remodel
Volume: ~29 staff per store × ~30–40 stores
Owner: Store Manager / L&amp;D
Participants: Store Manager (links to VS-07), L&amp;D (links to VS-19.4), IT (links to VS-27), Merchandising (links to VS-01), Change/PMO (links to VS-112)
Source: workflow W3490 — Remodel Staff Training &amp; Change Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3490_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3490_Lane1" name="L&amp;D">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3490_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3490_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3490_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3490_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3490_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3490_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3490_Start4" name="Pre re-opening (W3489); new systems/assortment">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3490_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3490_Task5" name="L&amp;D/Store Manager plan the remodel training: new POS/technology (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: L&amp;D/Store Manager plan the remodel training: new POS/technology (links to VS-08/W3486), new assortment/categories and product knowledge (links to VS-01/W3478), new layout/wayfinding, new service offers, and brand/customer-experience standards (links to VS-13); schedule pre-opening training
Responsible (R): L&amp;D / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Per remodel</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3490_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3490_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3490_Task6" name="L&amp;D/Merchandising/IT deliver training to store staff (and any new hires links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: L&amp;D/Merchandising/IT deliver training to store staff (and any new hires links to VS-19.1): classroom, on-the-job, vendor training (links to W1099), and quick-reference guides; verify competence/checkout readiness before re-opening
Responsible (R): L&amp;D / Merchandising / IT
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per remodel</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3490_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3490_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3490_Task7" name="Store Manager/Change Mgmt manage the change: communication, address staff…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Store Manager/Change Mgmt manage the change: communication, address staff concerns, reinforce new ways-of-working in the first weeks post re-opening (links to VS-103.2 EX), and capture adoption issues; feed training gaps to L&amp;D (links to VS-19.4)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Change Mgmt
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Post re-opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3490_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3490_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3490_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3490_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-558 (ensure controlled execution — Re-merchandising, Re-opening &amp; Remodel Performance Analytics (PA-109.3).) | - operational: reinforcement and on-floor coaching; operational: pre-opening verification
Owner: Store Manager / L&amp;D</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3490_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3490_Annotation9" targetRef="W3490_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
