    <bpmn:process id="W_W3491" name="W3491. Post-Remodel Sales Lift &amp; Performance Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Re-opening (W3489); monthly/quarterly cycle
Frequency: Monthly + 6/12-month milestone
Volume: All recently-remodeled stores
Owner: FP&amp;A / VP Store Operations
Participants: FP&amp;A (links to VS-17.4/VS-33.2), VP Store Operations, Merchandising (links to VS-01/VS-101), BI (links to VS-28.1), Regional Manager (links to VS-07)
Source: workflow W3491 — Post-Remodel Sales Lift &amp; Performance Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3491_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3491_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3491_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3491_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3491_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3491_Lane2" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3491_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3491_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3491_Start4" name="Re-opening (W3489); monthly/quarterly cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3491_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3491_Task5" name="FP&amp;A/BI track post-remodel performance: comp-sales lift vs pre-remodel baseline…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: FP&amp;A/BI track post-remodel performance: comp-sales lift vs pre-remodel baseline and vs non-remodeled control stores, traffic, ATV/basket, category mix (links to VS-01), gross margin (links to VS-101), inventory turn (links to VS-05), and conversion; normalize for seasonality and external factors
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A / BI
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3491_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3491_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3491_Task6" name="FP&amp;A/Merchandising reconcile actual lift to the business case (W3476)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: FP&amp;A/Merchandising reconcile actual lift to the business case (W3476): payback/IRR tracking, lost-sales recovery, and category-level contribution; identify laggards and root cause (assortment, pricing, marketing, macro)
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A / Merchandising
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3491_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3491_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3491_Task7" name="VP Store Operations/FP&amp;A report remodel performance to the program review…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VP Store Operations/FP&amp;A report remodel performance to the program review (W3496) and executives (links to VS-33.2), re-baseline laggards, and feed insights to future remodel concepts (W3475) and the roadmap (W3473/W3495)
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): COO / CFO
Duration: Quarterly/annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3491_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3491_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3491_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3491_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-558 (ensure controlled execution — Re-merchandising, Re-opening &amp; Remodel Performance Analytics (PA-109.3).) | - operational: control-store comparison; operational: root-cause and corrective action
Owner: FP&amp;A / VP Store Operations</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
