    <bpmn:process id="W_W3495" name="W3495. Store Refurbishment Cadence &amp; Lifecycle Refresh Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual planning (links to VS-33.1); lifecycle analytics (W3491)
Frequency: Annual + multi-year
Volume: ~200-store portfolio
Owner: VP Store Operations / Real Estate
Participants: VP Store Operations, Real Estate, Facilities (links to VS-20.3), Finance (links to VS-40/VS-17.4), Merchandising (links to VS-01)
Source: workflow W3495 — Store Refurbishment Cadence &amp; Lifecycle Refresh Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3495_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3495_Lane1" name="Real Estate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3495_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3495_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3495_Lane2" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3495_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3495_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3495_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3495_Start4" name="Annual planning (links to VS-33.1); lifecycle analytics (W3491)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3495_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3495_Task5" name="Real Estate/Facilities maintain the store-lifecycle and refurbishment-cadence…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Real Estate/Facilities maintain the store-lifecycle and refurbishment-cadence model: per-store age, last-remodel date, fixture/MEP condition, comp trajectory (links to W3474), and the tiered refresh plan (full remodel / refresh / re-fixture / repaint-and-repair); forecast the multi-year refresh demand
Responsible (R): Real Estate / Facilities
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3495_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3495_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3495_Task6" name="VP Store Operations/Finance balance the refresh cadence against the capital…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Store Operations/Finance balance the refresh cadence against the capital plan (links to VS-40/VS-33.1) and new-store growth (links to VS-37): optimize the mix of full remodels vs light refreshes vs re-fixtures to maximize portfolio ROI under the capex constraint
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Finance
Accountable (A): COO / CFO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3495_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3495_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3495_Task7" name="VP Store Operations/Real Estate publish the multi-year refresh roadmap and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VP Store Operations/Real Estate publish the multi-year refresh roadmap and integrate to the store-lifecycle strategy (W3473), new-store (links to VS-37) and closure (links to VS-59) plans, and the capex portfolio (links to VS-40/VS-112); refresh annually with performance data (W3491)
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Real Estate
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3495_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3495_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3495_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
