    <bpmn:process id="W_W3496" name="W3496. Store Format Innovation &amp; Remodel Program Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual strategy review; board/exec cycle (links to VS-33/VS-36)
Frequency: Annual + quarterly
Volume: Program-wide
Owner: VP Store Operations / COO
Participants: VP Store Operations, COO, CFO, CMO, Real Estate, Merchandising (links to VS-01), Strategy (links to VS-33), PMO (links to VS-112)
Source: workflow W3496 — Store Format Innovation &amp; Remodel Program Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3496_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3496_Lane1" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3496_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3496_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3496_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3496_Lane2" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3496_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3496_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3496_Start4" name="Annual strategy review; board/exec cycle (links to VS-33/VS-36)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3496_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3496_Task5" name="VP Store Operations/Merchandising drive store-format innovation: pilot new…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VP Store Operations/Merchandising drive store-format innovation: pilot new concepts/formats (e.g., appliance-gallery format, project-design center links to VS-66, renewable/solar bay links to VS-70/VS-108, digital-first store links to VS-75), test in a remodel, and scale successful concepts into the standard; benchmark competitors and global retail (links to VS-33.3)
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Merchandising / Store Design
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3496_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3496_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3496_Task6" name="VP Store Operations/PMO conduct the quarterly remodel-program review: portfolio…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Store Operations/PMO conduct the quarterly remodel-program review: portfolio progress (links to VS-112), performance vs business case (W3491/W3561), capex variance (W3493), lessons (W3494), refresh cadence (W3495), and vendor/design performance (links to VS-67); decide adjustments and resource allocation
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / PMO
Accountable (A): COO / CFO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3496_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3496_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3496_Task7" name="COO/CFO report the remodel program (performance, capex, format innovation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: COO/CFO report the remodel program (performance, capex, format innovation, store-lifecycle health) to the executive committee (links to VS-33.2) and Board (links to VS-36); ensure alignment with corporate strategy, capital, and store-growth plans and approve policy/standard updates
Responsible (R): COO / CFO
Accountable (A): CEO / Board
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3496_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3496_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3496_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3496_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-136 (ensure remodel capex &amp; handover control.) | - operational: piloting and benchmarking; operational: quarterly governance and board oversight
Owner: VP Store Operations / COO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
